    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## DUNCAN RUNTIME LEARNING R01 — EXACT-HEAD VERIFICATION RECEIPT\n\nHEAD = `a58e4eb0a2e6987c309e3f1105c18382c979527b`\nBASE = `main@b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\n\n### ROOT CAUSE\nFortress R01 proved learning persistence/rebuildability, but the live bootstrap did not require consumption of `DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT.json` before tool/action selection. Persistence PASS was therefore not runtime-learning PASS. The active Night School scheduler was also absent/stale; archive context had stopped at 2026-08-31.\n\n### REPAIR ON THIS HEAD\n- `AGENTS.md` now requires fresh consumption of `zb-archive-v1:hq/archive-v1/derived/duncan-night-v1/DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT.json` before substantive action selection.\n- Decision gate = `OWNER_INTENT -> DURABLE_STATE -> RELEVANT_LEARNING -> ANTI_REGRESSION_CHECK -> ACTION`.\n- Direct OWNER correction applies immediately; Night School consolidates later.\n- Regression contract/test covers persistence-vs-consumption and known failure classes including tool-before-task, non-image imagegen, overformalization and stale-route resurrection.\n- Existing `.gitleaksignore` mechanism was extended only for three exact historical false-positive fingerprints after direct source inspection proved they are a commit SHA in an `*_HEAD` field, an NPZ dictionary key, and the production phrase `KEY POSES -> EXPOSURE/TIMING`; no broad rule suppression was added.\n\n### FRESH LEARNING EVIDENCE\nPR #111 comment `5506834354` = `DNR01-20260902-011`, deliberately records `owner_intent_execution_discipline: UNTESTED -> FAILED`; no fake skill PASS.\nPermanent Archive accepted it; current derived context contains `LEARNING_CONSUMPTION_RULE`, `TOOL_CLASSIFICATION_RULE`, `SIMPLE_GOAL_RULE`, `IMMEDIATE_CORRECTION_RULE`, and `RESULT_OVER_PROCESS` as a supporting OWNER-taste signal.\nDaily `Duncan Anime Night School` scheduling has been restored separately; same-session correction does not wait for it.\n\n### EXACT-HEAD CI\n- `hq-validate` run `33610250828` / #910 = SUCCESS.\n- `oss-security` run `33610250819` / #240 = SUCCESS.\n- Prior oss-security failure `33609891507` was diagnosed, not blindly retried: Gitleaks found three pre-existing historical generic-api-key false positives dated 2026-08-30/31. Exact-source inspection proved all three non-secret; existing fingerprint allowlist path was reused.\n\n### CLAIM BOUNDARY\n`IMPLEMENTATION_EXACT_HEAD_VERIFICATION = PASS`\n`ARCHIVE_LEARNING_UPDATE = PROVEN`\n`DAILY_NIGHT_SCHOOL_SCHEDULE = RESTORED`\n`MODEL_WEIGHT_TRAINING = NO / NOT CLAIMED`\n`PRIME_CORE_MUTATION = NO`\n`CANON_OR_PRODUCTION_AUTHORITY_MUTATION = NO`\n`RUNTIME_LEARNING_BEHAVIOR_GENERALIZATION = NOT YET PROVEN ACROSS MULTIPLE FUTURE CASES`\n\nMerge/installing the bootstrap hook is necessary for future sessions to consume the learned context, but merge itself must not be reported as proof that all future behavioral regressions are impossible.",
